# Cloudflare Workers Assets default Cache-Control is
# `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`. Hashed Vite files are content-
# addressed — long-cache them so mobile Safari does not re-download the
# main graph on every visit. Applied by the asset store itself (see
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/).
# Worker `withHashedAssetCache` is the run_worker_first backup.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Security headers on every Assets-served path (security audit 2026-11-14, H2).
# Worker / Express responses get the same set from
# artifacts/api-server/src/lib/securityHeaders.ts; test/securityHeaders.test.ts
# keeps the two in sync. The CSP is Report-Only on purpose (see that file).
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
